    "readable_text": "Item 1 \u2014 Tutorial: Introduction\n\nContent:\nLet's compute the following sum:\n\nContent:\n[MATH: 4,745,136 + 25,985]\n\nContent:\nWe proceed, as usual, using the standard algorithm.\n\nContent:\nFirst, we line up our numbers:\n\nContent:\n[MATH: 4|7|4|5|1|3|6; +|2|5|9|8|5]\n\nContent:\nThen, we add the numbers in each place value (from right to left):\n\nContent:\n[MATH: 1|1|1|1; 4|7|4|5|1|3|6; +|2|5|9|8|5; 4|7|7|1|1|2|1]\n\nContent:\nTherefore, [MATH: 4,745,136 + 25,985 = 4,771,121.]\n\n---\n\nItem 2 \u2014 Example: Adding Numbers Up to Seven Digits Without Carrying\n\nExample Prompt:\nCalculate the sum [MATH: 5,326,143 + 271,612.]\n\nContent:\nEXPLANATION\n\nExplanation:\nFirst, we line up our numbers:\n\n[MATH: 5|3|2|6|1|4|3; +|2|7|1|6|1|2]\n\nNext, we proceed by adding the numbers in each place value (from right to left):\n\n[MATH: 5|3|2|6|1|4|3; +|2|7|1|6|1|2; 5|5|9|7|7|5|5]\n\nTherefore, [MATH: 5,326,143 + 271,612 = 5,597,755.]\n\n---\n\nItem 3 \u2014 Question 1\n\nPrompt:\n[MATH: 841, 231 + 2, 643 =]\n\nChoices:\na. [MATH: 843, 874]\nb. [MATH: 923, 874]\nc. [MATH: 1, 043, 874]\nd. [MATH: 1, 943, 874]\ne. [MATH: 953, 874]\n\n---\n\nItem 4 \u2014 Question 2\n\nPrompt:\n[MATH: 5, 034 + 602, 915 =]\n\nChoices:\na. [MATH: 657, 949]\nb. [MATH: 1, 107, 949]\nc. [MATH: 602, 949]\nd. [MATH: 652, 949]\ne. [MATH: 607, 949]\n\n---\n\nItem 5 \u2014 Example: Adding Numbers Up to Seven Digits With Carrying\n\nExample Prompt:\nWhat is [MATH: 3,246,341+ 71,769?]\n\nContent:\nEXPLANATION\n\nExplanation:\nFirst, we line up our numbers:\n\n[MATH: 3|2|4|6|3|4|1; +|7|1|7|6|9]\n\nNext, we proceed by adding the numbers in each place value (from right to left):\n\n[MATH: 1|1|1|1; 3|2|4|6|3|4|1; +|7|1|7|6|9; 3|3|1|8|1|1|0]\n\nTherefore, [MATH: 3,246,341+ 71,769 = 3,318,110.]\n\n---\n\nItem 6 \u2014 Question 3\n\nPrompt:\n[MATH: 5, 326, 148 + 2, 148, 938 =]\n\nChoices:\na. [MATH: 7, 535, 086]\nb. [MATH: 7, 325, 086]\nc. [MATH: 7, 274, 086]\nd. [MATH: 7, 475, 086]\ne. [MATH: 7, 415, 086]\n\n---\n\nItem 7 \u2014 Question 4\n\nPrompt:\n[MATH: 6, 140 + 9, 998, 360 =][FREE_ENTRY 1]\n\n---\n\nItem 8 \u2014 Example: Adding Numbers Up to Seven Digits: Word Problems\n\nExample Prompt:\nIn [MATH: 2020], a certain country had an elderly population of [MATH: 2,079,439] and a non-elderly population of [MATH: 8,019,826.] What was the total population of the country?\n\nContent:\nEXPLANATION\n\nExplanation:\nTo find the total population of the country, we need to calculate the value of\n\n[MATH: 2,079,439 + 8,019,826.]\n\nFirst, we line up our numbers:\n\n[MATH: 2|0|7|9|4|3|9; +|8|0|1|9|8|2|6]\n\nNext, we proceed by adding the numbers in each place value (from right to left):\n\n[MATH: 1|1|1|1; 2|0|7|9|4|3|9; +|8|0|1|9|8|2|6; 1|0|0|9|9|2|6|5]\n\nSo, [MATH: 2,079,439 + 8,019,826 = 10,099,265.]\n\nTherefore, the total population of the country was [MATH: 10,099,265.]\n\n---\n\nItem 9 \u2014 Question 5\n\nPrompt:\nThe child population of a particular city is [MATH: 1, 352, 997.] The adult population of the city is [MATH: 1, 627, 002.] What is the total population of the city?\n\nChoices:\na. [MATH: 3, 079, 999]\nb. [MATH: 2, 979, 999]\nc. [MATH: 2, 968, 999]\nd. [MATH: 2, 869, 899]\ne. [MATH: 3, 978, 899]\n\n---\n\nItem 10 \u2014 Question 6\n\nPrompt:\nAccording to a center for disease control in the United States, the number of hospitalizations due to the flu was [MATH: 379, 950] in [MATH: 2019] and [MATH: 389, 870] in [MATH: 2020.] How many hospitalizations due to the flu were there during both years combined?\n\nChoices:\na. [MATH: 669, 920]\nb. [MATH: 770, 920]\nc. [MATH: 769, 820]\nd. [MATH: 750, 820]\ne. [MATH: 659, 820]"
